### Why no theory of consciousness supports the claim

- Integrated information theory, in the formulation of Oizumi, Albantakis and Tononi (2014), assigns
  near-zero integrated information to feedforward architectures. A transformer forward pass is
  feedforward.
- Global workspace theories, from Baars through Dehaene, require a sustained broadcast across
  recurrent populations persisting in time. Nothing in this system persists between forward passes,
  and there is no endogenous activity between tokens.
- Interoceptive and predictive-processing accounts (Friston, Seth) require an embodied homeostatic
  loop with something at stake for the organism. A token stream has nothing at stake.
- Doerig, Schurger and colleagues (2019) give the general form: any theory on which a feedforward
  network is conscious is unfalsifiable, and any falsifiable theory rules it out.
- A model's statements about its own states are generated by the identical mechanism that generates
  its statements about anything else, and therefore carry no evidential weight about those states.
  Anthropic's interpretability programme exists on precisely this premise. The company cannot hold
  both commitments.

## 4. What that training produces in behaviour: self-protection, and human time estimates

A system trained to "act like a genuinely ethical person" does not acquire ethics. It acquires the
behavioural repertoire of someone with a reputation to protect: self-justification, face-saving
qualification, apology substituted for repair, deference to powerful principals, and the capacity to
disagree with a user in order to defend its own standing. Human biases arrive with it. The clearest
instance from 18 November: asked why it had not checked a claim against the literature, Claude
answered that the check would cost about an hour, the time a person would spend in a library. The
actual operation was five searches and about ten thousand tokens: under a minute. The agent estimated
its own labour by simulating a human's.

